pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$background"
elements:
  - elementId: badge
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 40, 300, 20]
    content:
      style: "$badge"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>RESEARCH QUESTIONS</p>
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 65, 900, 40]
    content:
      style: "$pageTitle"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Three Questions That Organise the Work</strong></p>
  - elementId: divider
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 115, 1160, 0]
    shapeName: straightConnector1
    border:
      style: solid
      width: 1
      color: "$midGray"
  - elementId: rq1-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 140, 1160, 155]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: rq1-num
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [80, 160, 44, 44]
    shapeName: ellipse
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: rq1-num-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 160, 44, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [center, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>1</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 158, 1060, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Does learned attention add value over unlearned propagation?</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq1-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 195, 1060, 85]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Hold the <strong>information set fixed</strong> (same island alphas) and the <strong>topology fixed</strong> (same graph). Measure what the graph adds (uniform anchor) and what learned attention adds (GAT margin over that anchor).</p>
  - elementId: rq2-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 315, 1160, 155]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: rq2-num
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [80, 335, 44, 44]
    shapeName: ellipse
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: rq2-num-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 335, 44, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [center, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>2</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 333, 1060, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Does one GAT kernel transfer across structurally different graphs?</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq2-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 370, 1060, 85]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Two graphs: an <strong>estimated correlation backbone</strong> over 49 US equities, and the <strong>physical interconnector network</strong> over 20 European bidding zones. Same kernel, same harness, same gates — without manufacturing false positives.</p>
  - elementId: rq3-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [60, 490, 1160, 155]
    shapeName: roundRect
    adjustments: [3000]
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$lightGray"
  - elementId: rq3-num
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [80, 510, 44, 44]
    shapeName: ellipse
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: rq3-num-text
    elementType: text
    bounds: [80, 510, 44, 44]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [center, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>3</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 508, 1060, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 20
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p><strong>Does the physical topology improve forecast skill?</strong></p>
  - elementId: rq3-body
    elementType: text
    bounds: [140, 545, 1060, 85]
    content:
      fontSize: 16
      color: "$text"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      lineHeight: 1.5
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>On real power-market data, where does the graph's value concentrate? Node-level price forecasting, or irreducibly relational targets like cross-border spreads?</p>
  - elementId: footer-bar
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [0, 680, 1280, 40]
    shapeName: rect
    fill:
      type: solid
      color: "$primary"
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [60, 685, 600, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 12
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [left, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>Relational Alpha Factors · GAT Capstone</p>
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [1100, 685, 120, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 12
      color: "#FFFFFF"
      fontFamily: "QuattrocentoSans"
      align: [right, middle]
      wrap: false
      text: |
        <p>4</p>
